maya: Heads-up — sample-app rerank + batching helper is returning inconsistent embedding dims when I batch 3 docs together. repro below.
kevin: Which SDK + version? can you paste the raw response?
maya: node sdk v0.7.1, sampleapp default batching helper. Raw response shows first two embeddings length 1536, last one 1535. Not a model fallback — embeddings present but one value missing. :thinking:
maya: Raw HTTP body (trimmed):
```json
{
  "results": [
    {"id":"a", "embedding": [0.12, 0.03, /* ... total 1536 floats ... */]},
    {"id":"b", "embedding": [0.11, 0.04, /* ... total 1536 floats ... */]},
    {"id":"c", "embedding": [0.09, 0.01, /* ... total 1535 floats (missing last) ... */]}
  ]
}
```
sam: Is this happening only when using the batching helper or also when you call the embeddings endpoint per-item?
maya: Only when batching. Per-item calls return 1536 each. Also not a retry — single request, no 5xx.
maya: Snippet of the helper (simplified):
```js
function packEmbeddings(items) {
  const out = new Float32Array(items.length * 1536);
  let off = 0;
  for (const v of items) {
    out.set(v, off); // v is a Float32Array from model response
    off += v.length;
  }
  return out;
}
```
maya: My suspicion: last vector got one element trimmed when using `set` if `v.length` mismatches typed array expectations — maybe off-by-one in the helper that builds the request/response mapping.
kevin: That matches a bug we had in a different SDK: when concatenating `Uint8Array` slices we accidentally passed an end index inclusive. Node slice semantics? :eyes:
lina: tagging @eng-ml and @eng-platform for visibility — could be SDK parity or sampleapp helper bug.
ci-bot: CI: sampleapp unit tests failing on "embeddings-batch-shape" in branch maya/batch-dim-fix — 1 failing test.
sam: Quick mitigation: validate length per embedding after unpacking and pad with zeros if shorter, then raise a warning. Will open a small PR against sampleapp and add an assertion test.
kevin: If it's in SDK helper we should ship a patch release. If only sampleapp, update docs and add test. Either way we need a reproducible test and the failing request id.
maya: request_id: rq_0bX9fDk2. I pushed a repro in sampleapp under `examples/batch-dim-repro` with failing test. PR in a bit.
maya: Thanks — will follow up once PR is up, leaving here for triage. :thumbsup:
